kind how-do-i
title How do I create a new look?
intro A look is a font set, a size and a color scheme. A new look goes into the draft when you save, and the console uses it once a terminal uses the look and you install the draft.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose New look.
3. Erase the name.
4. Type Monoid-Nerd.
5. Press Enter.
6. Set Font set to mono.
7. Choose Size.
8. Choose 16 pt.
9. Press Esc.
10. Press s to save.
at the save
check screen shows "Monoid-Nerd"
check draft look Monoid-Nerd font-name mono
check draft look Monoid-Nerd font-size 16
check installed lacks "Monoid-Nerd"
